ZapCash started as a small rewards site and is being rebuilt as something people actually need: a calm, honest view of where their money goes, made for Nigerian banks and Nigerian habits.

The first milestone is live: the landing page, sign in with Google or email, the app shell with Home, Activity, Plan and Me, light and dark themes, and the sync layer that keeps a private SQL copy of your data in the browser. Next come statement import for GTBank, Opay, Kuda, Moniepoint and the other big banks, the bank charges tracker, and Ask ZapCash, where you can type "How much did I spend on transport last month?" or "Wetin I spend for data this year?" and get a straight answer.
